==English==

===Etymology===
Morphologically {{suffix|en|our|selves}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/aʊəˈsɛlvz/|/ɑːˈsɛlvz/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/aʊɚˈsɛlvz/|/ɑɹˈsɛlvz/|a=GenAm}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-ourselves.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛlvz|s=2}}

===Pronoun===
{{en-pron|desc=first personal plural pronoun|reflexive case of|we}}

# {{lb|en|reflexive}} [[us|Us]]; {{non-gloss|the group including the speaker as the object of a verb or preposition when that group also is the subject.}}
#: {{ux|en|We should keep this for '''ourselves'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|Let's not beat '''ourselves''' up over this.}}
# {{lb|en|emphatic}} {{non-gloss|Intensifies the subject as the group including the speaker, especially to indicate that no one else satisfies the predicate or needs to be included.}}
#: {{ux|en|We did it '''ourselves'''.}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial}} {{non-gloss|Referring to everyone being addressed.}}
#: {{ux|en|Come on everyone! Let's get '''ourselves''' up and out of bed, please.|q=''reflexive''}}
#: {{ux|en|No talking now boys and girls, and no asking our friends for help. We should be able to work this out '''ourselves'''.|q = ''emphatic''}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial|may seem patronising}} {{non-gloss|Referring to an individual person being addressed, especially a person in the speaker's care.}}
#: {{ux|en|Hello Mrs Miggins. Did we manage to wash '''ourselves''' this morning?|q=''reflexive''}}
#: {{ux|en|Well done Timmy! Did we make that model '''ourselves'''?|q = ''emphatic''}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|usself}} {{q|obsolete or dialectal}}
